DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     These functions operate on IEEE EUI-64s using an _e_u_i_6_4 structure, which
     is defined in the header file <_s_y_s_/_e_u_i_6_4_._h>:

           /*
            * The number of bytes in an EUI-64.
            */
           #define EUI64_LEN               8

           /*
            * Structure of an IEEE EUI-64.
            */
           struct  eui64 {
                   u_char octet[EUI64_LEN];
           };

     The eeuuii6644__aattoonn() function converts an ASCII representation of an EUI-64
     into an _e_u_i_6_4 structure.  Likewise, eeuuii6644__nnttooaa() converts an EUI-64 spec‐
     ified as an _e_u_i_6_4 structure into an ASCII string.

     The eeuuii6644__nnttoohhoosstt() and eeuuii6644__hhoossttttoonn() functions map EUI-64s to their
     corresponding hostnames as specified in the _/_e_t_c_/_e_u_i_6_4 database.  The
     eeuuii6644__nnttoohhoosstt() function converts from EUI-64 to hostname, and
     eeuuii6644__hhoossttttoonn() converts from hostname to EUI-64.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, eeuuii6644__nnttooaa() returns a pointer to a string containing an
     ASCII representation of an EUI-64.  If it is unable to convert the sup‐
     plied _e_u_i_6_4 structure, it returns a NULL pointer.  Likewise, eeuuii6644__aattoonn()
     returns a pointer to an _e_u_i_6_4 structure on success and a NULL pointer on
     failure.

     The eeuuii6644__nnttoohhoosstt() and eeuuii6644__hhoossttttoonn() functions both return zero on
     success or non-zero if they were unable to find a match in the _/_e_t_c_/_e_u_i_6_4
     database.

NNOOTTEESS
     The user must ensure that the hostname strings passed to the
     eeuuii6644__nnttoohhoosstt() and eeuuii6644__hhoossttttoonn() functions are large enough to contain
     the returned hostnames.

